<title>UK: Rutland confirms it not eyeing Simon.</title>
<headline>Rutland confirms it not eyeing Simon.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rutland Trust Plc confirmed on Thursday it had not made a takeover approach to Simon Engineering Plc.</p>
<p>It did reveal that it has had informal discussions with Simon regarding its storage and port activities.</p>
<p>Simon, a British engineering company, earlier issued a statement denying newspaper speculation that it had received a takeover approach.</p>
<p>Rutland, whose operations range from corporate finance and investment to container port operations and professional services, is 11 percent owned by Belgium's Brederode SA.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
